#!/bin/bash
# Test-build every DKMS module against an incoming linux-headers package before pacman
# installs it. Run by 01-dkms-precheck.hook (PreTransaction, AbortOnFail): one failed build
# aborts the whole upgrade and leaves the system as it was.
#
# The build runs in a private mount namespace. Overlays put the new headers under
# /usr/lib/modules and catch all writes to /var/lib/dkms and /usr/src, so nothing touches
# the real system. Modules whose Makefiles hard-code /lib/modules/<kver>/build still work.
#
#   dkms-precheck                    hook mode: reads pacman targets on stdin
#   dkms-precheck <headers.pkg.tar>  test a package file by hand
#   touch /etc/dkms-precheck.skip    skip the check once (the file is removed)
set -uo pipefail

if [[ -e /etc/dkms-precheck.skip ]]; then
  rm -f /etc/dkms-precheck.skip
  echo "==> dkms-precheck: skipped once (/etc/dkms-precheck.skip)"
  exit 0
fi

pkg=${1:-}
if [[ -z $pkg ]]; then
  grep -qx linux-headers || exit 0
  ver=$(pacman -Si linux-headers 2>/dev/null | awk '/^Version/ {print $3; exit}')
  for d in $(pacman-conf CacheDir); do
    for f in "$d"/linux-headers-"$ver"-x86_64.pkg.tar.*; do
      [[ -f $f && $f != *.sig ]] && pkg=$f
    done
  done
  if [[ -z $pkg ]]; then
    echo "==> dkms-precheck: no cached linux-headers $ver package found. Upgrade aborted."
    echo "==> To upgrade without the check: sudo touch /etc/dkms-precheck.skip, then rerun."
    exit 1
  fi
fi

tmp=$(mktemp -d /var/tmp/dkms-precheck.XXXXXX)
trap 'umount -R "$tmp/mnt" 2>/dev/null; rm -rf "$tmp"' EXIT
mkdir -p "$tmp"/{new,logs,mnt}
bsdtar -xf "$pkg" -C "$tmp/new" usr/lib/modules || { echo "==> dkms-precheck: cannot read $pkg"; exit 1; }
kver=$(ls "$tmp/new/usr/lib/modules")
mods=()
for src in /var/lib/dkms/*/*/source; do
  [[ -e $src ]] || continue
  mv=${src#/var/lib/dkms/}; mods+=("${mv%/source}")
done
echo "==> dkms-precheck: test-building ${#mods[@]} DKMS modules for $kver"

# Inside the namespace: overlay the three trees, then build each module.
unshare -m --propagation private bash -s "$tmp" "$kver" "${mods[@]}" <<'NS'
tmp=$1 kver=$2; shift 2
ov() {  # ov <dir> <name> [extra lower]
  mkdir -p "$tmp/mnt/$2"/{up,work}
  mount -t overlay overlay -o "lowerdir=${3:+$3:}$1,upperdir=$tmp/mnt/$2/up,workdir=$tmp/mnt/$2/work" "$1"
}
ov /usr/lib/modules modules "$tmp/new/usr/lib/modules" || exit 2
ov /var/lib/dkms dkms || exit 2
ov /usr/src src || exit 2
fail=0
for mv in "$@"; do
  m=${mv%/*} v=${mv#*/}
  dkms build -m "$m" -v "$v" -k "$kver" --force >"$tmp/logs/$m.log" 2>&1
  rc=$?
  if [[ $rc = 0 ]]; then
    echo "    ok      $m $v"
  elif [[ $rc = 77 ]]; then
    echo "    skipped $m $v (dkms.conf excludes $kver)"
  else
    echo "    FAILED  $m $v"
    tail -n 15 "$tmp/logs/$m.log" | sed 's/^/        /'
    log=$(ls -t /var/lib/dkms/"$m"/"$v"/build/make.log 2>/dev/null | head -1)
    [[ -n $log ]] && grep -m 5 -E "error" "$log" | sed 's/^/        /'
    fail=1
  fi
done
exit $fail
NS
rc=$?

if [[ $rc != 0 ]]; then
  echo "==> dkms-precheck: a DKMS module does not build for $kver. Upgrade aborted; nothing changed."
  echo "==> Keep the working kernel and upgrade everything else:"
  echo "==>   sudo pacman -Syu --ignore linux,linux-headers"
  echo "==> Then fix the module (or wait for an update) and run the full upgrade again."
  exit 1
fi
echo "==> dkms-precheck: all modules build for $kver"
